<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.toByteArray().length; \result.toByteArray()[i] == (i < bb.limit() ? bb.array()[bb.position() + i] : 0);</code>

This assert statement ensures that the resulting `BitSet` is not null and that each byte in its byte array representation matches the corresponding byte in the `ByteBuffer` `bb` from index 0 up to the size of the byte array. Note that if `i` exceeds `bb.limit()`, the byte in the resulting `BitSet` should be 0, which is handled by the conditional expression in the assertion.
